## Bug Fixes

- Reworked Floyd-Steinberg depth dithering to diffuse errors in plain `0..255` RGB channel space, avoiding the previous linear/sRGB conversion mismatch that could smear or "melt" reduced-color output.
- Improved `Ctrl+S` save feedback: successful hotkey saves now keep the spinner/wait cursor visible briefly (minimum hold duration) so save confirmation remains noticeable even on very fast writes.
- Fixed curve edit handles so they stay on-curve while dragging, and dragging a handle no longer drags other control points with it.
- Fixed erratic shape handle dragging by basing move/resize/path edits on a cached drag-start shape snapshot instead of cumulative deltas.
- Fixed shape handle stability across repeated rotate/resize/move operations: rotated resizes now render every frame (no null first frame), path-handle drags bake rotation into geometry for consistent behavior, rotated polyline resizes preserve open/closed state, and shape drags use sub-pixel mouse coordinates to prevent handle jumps.
- Fixed severe performance drops while dragging polygon/curve path handles by reusing path-handle DOM nodes (no rebuild per mousemove), caching active-shape bounds, and batching handle updates to `requestAnimationFrame`.
- Added strict pixel snapping for vector-shape translation only: dragging the selection box to move a whole shape rounds X/Y to integers, while rotation and vertex/path handle edits remain high-precision floats.
- Fixed Smart Pencil-created editable shapes not responding to brush size hotkeys: `Ctrl+Plus/Minus` now updates the active shape stroke width while it is in shape edit mode.
- Fixed larger shape and Smart Pencil shape strokes inheriting anti-aliased edge pixels from the round brush cache, restoring hard same-color pixels.
- Reduced inconsistent transform lag spikes by throttling the rotate-handle pixel-sampled inversion (avoids repeated `getImageData()` readbacks) and skipping path-handle relayout when only shape translation changed.
- Declared the `--sel-rotate-icon-color` CSS custom property in `:root` to resolve editor/lint "Cannot resolve custom property" warnings for the rotate-handle SVG color variable.
- Improved selection-rotation precision significantly by switching rotate-drag input to sub-pixel mouse coordinates, using continuous unwrapped angle accumulation (no Â±180Ã‚Â° clamp during a drag), and adding radius-scaled sensitivity for finer low-radius control.
- Fixed undo/redo behavior when starting a new rectangular selection after an undo: creating/selecting no longer truncates redo history by itself; redo is preserved until the selection causes an actual document change (move/transform/commit/delete).
- Fixed selection-rotation handle rendering orientation in the new CleanEdge path by correcting the texture upload Y-flip state (removed mirrored/vertical-flipped preview behavior that inverted perceived rotate direction).
- Fixed selection-rotation handle drag math so rotation direction now follows cursor direction, and made repeated handle drags continue from the current rotation instead of resetting to default on re-click.
- Fixed rotated selection border thickness scaling by making the rotated-border stroke/inset use inverse zoom, keeping it visually ~1px in screen space like other selection overlays.
- Fixed rotated selection border zoom behavior more robustly by replacing CSS border-based stroke with inverse-zoom gradient edge lines (avoids browser border-width clamping under transform so the frame stays ~1px on screen).
- Fixed rotated rectangular selection border rendering to show all four edges with alternating colors (top/bottom/left/right) while rotating.
- Fixed high-zoom (>200%) rotated-border dropout on right/bottom edges by moving the rotated frame to a dedicated inverse-scaled overlay element (`#sel-rot-border`) instead of drawing directly on the hit-area box.
- Fixed selection resize-handle blurriness at certain fractional zoom levels by snapping handle centers to screen pixels (prevents 1px borders landing on half-pixels and anti-aliasing).
- Fixed rotated complex/masked selections to keep using ants outlines and rotate ants with the selection instead of falling back to a rectangular rotated border.
- Fixed selection handle blur by snapping handle placement to screen pixels while keeping handles stage-relative, and kept the rotate handle icon size constant across zoom.
- Fixed selection/path handles not tracking the canvas in free (unanchored) mode after the recent handle changes.
- Hardened rotate-release click suppression so the next stray click after rotating a selection or editable shape is consumed instead of sometimes deselecting the active transform.
- Fixed `Ctrl` rotation snapping so selections and editable shapes now snap to absolute world axes/octants (`0, 45, 90...`) instead of snapping relative to the angle where the drag started.
- Added a Debug-only `Smart Pencil: Curve only` toggle that constrains Smart Pencil detection to cubic curves, skipping line/polygon/circle/ellipse snapping when enabled.
- Adjusted `Smart Pencil: Curve only` so it always converts the stroke into a cubic curve, including strokes that look like closed shapes, instead of falling back to freehand.
- Moved the `Smart Pencil: Curve only` toggle from Debug to Misc so it sits with normal utility controls instead of debug-only tools.
- Moved the `Undo history` controls from Debug to Misc so both utility cards live in the regular Misc toolbar.
- Fixed the selection rotate-handle CSS variable reference typo so `--sel-rotate-icon-color` resolves correctly again.
- Fixed desktop relaunch behavior for single-instance mode: clicking the desktop shortcut or taskbar app entry now opens a new CDPaint window instead of only focusing the existing one.
- Fixed Magic Wand right-click interaction: right-click now directly toggles wand mode (contiguous/global) and selects Wand immediately, without opening the dropdown menu.
- Fixed picker tool return behavior so after sampling a color it restores the last drawing tool including Fill (bucket) and shape tools, while not switching to non-drawing tools like Zoom/Wand.
- Fixed selection-move preview transparency mismatch: when Transparent Selection is enabled, drag/move preview now honors Color 2 transparency the same way as the final committed selection.
- Fixed crop behavior so it no longer keys out Color 2 transparency while cropping, preventing Color 2 pixels from being erased during crop.
- Fixed transparent Color 2 tolerance handling so a zero tolerance stays zero instead of falling back to a default when pasting or rendering selections.
- Fixed auto-paste transparency re-keying after color-mode conversion: when tolerance is zero, the post-conversion pass no longer removes newly quantized colors.
- Fixed paste transparency keying to use a pre-conversion mask, preventing color-mode conversion from turning unrelated colors transparent.
- Set the default transparent selection tolerance to 0 so only exact Color 2 matches are keyed unless changed.
- Fixed selection preview blurring at zoomed-out levels by snapping the draw position/size to screen pixels for crisp rendering.
- Fixed a Windows maximized-window hitbox issue where the invisible top resize strip could intercept clicks near custom top-right title controls (close/maximize). Switched to native no-shadow windows (`shadow: false`) so custom title bar layout stays unchanged and drag-to-restore still works.
- Fixed maximize/restore title button state desync after drag-to-restore from maximized by refreshing the maximize icon on window resize events.
- Fixed stale top-left title bar app icon by removing the hardcoded embedded base64 image and loading `src/app-icon.png` so the custom title bar icon stays in sync with current project icon assets.
- Fixed maximized window restore behavior on Windows so persisted startup state no longer applies normal size/position before maximize, preventing a visible resize border/frame when opening in maximized mode.
- Fixed a remaining Windows frameless maximize border case for file-opened secondary windows by syncing `resizable` with maximize state (`false` when maximized, restored to `true` after unmaximize).
- Enforced a minimum desktop window size of `400x400` (main window and file-opened secondary windows), with startup size restore clamped to that minimum.
- Updated `F11` fullscreen behavior to center the app window on-screen before entering fullscreen (and recenter after exiting), preventing off-screen window state from trapping the UI.
- Restored maximized frameless title-bar interaction on Windows by keeping maximized windows resizable (fixes drag/minimize controls becoming unresponsive).
- Fixed modal backdrop-close behavior while Theme Colors is open so clicking outside other dialogs no longer auto-closes them during theme editing.
- Reverted the ribbon Color Mode buttons from PNG icon labels back to simple text labels (`24bpp`, `16bpp`, `15bpp`, `8bpp`, `4bpp`, `1bpp`) for the previous simpler UI.
- Fixed free-form lasso selection cancelling when the mouse is released outside the canvas by recording a clamped release point before finalizing the selection.
- Changed selection and shape rotation `Ctrl` snapping to the common 8 axes (`45deg` increments) instead of fine 1-degree steps.
- Fixed selection handle icon blur/soft edges across zoom levels by replacing center-translate counter-scaling with pixel-aligned inverse-scale positioning for the selection handles and rotate handle.
- Switched selection resize handles from a CSS background image to explicit `<img>` icons sized in inverse-zoom layout units, to avoid browser blur/resampling on the handle artwork at different zoom levels.
- Moved selection controls/handles out of the zoom-scaled stage into viewport screen space so the resize handles stay true `6x6` screen pixels at every zoom level without transform blur or color softening.
- Fixed modal input capture while Theme Colors is open by making dialog backdrops non-blocking in that mode, allowing simultaneous interaction with Theme Colors, other dialogs, and main UI.
- Added a basic undo-history cap for RAM efficiency: document undo now defaults to a 50-state limit, trims oldest snapshots automatically, and exposes a simple Debug tab toggle + value control backed by local storage.

